celld patch 0002: per-connection deterministic execution context.

Why. Chronolog Spec 10 executes each replicated transaction with the engine's
non-SQL inputs pinned: the clock, the PRNG, the timezone and the per-statement
counters. Chronolog's addon pins them process-wide (a wrapper default VFS,
SQLITE_TESTCTRL_PRNG_SEED, SQLITE_TESTCTRL_LOCALTIME_FAULT). celld runs many
cells on many threads, so every one of those must be per connection. This patch
adds sqlite3.pDetCtx, set with sqlite3_doltlite_set_det_context() and cleared
with sqlite3_doltlite_clear_det_context() (or at close). While it is set, only
that connection sees:

  1. the clock: every 'now'/date function (sqlite3StmtCurrentTime) and every
     Dolt timestamp (commit, merge, cherry-pick, revert, rebase commits, the
     dolt_diff/dolt_log working-set slice time, and the tag time, which used
     libc time(0)) goes through sqlite3DbCurrentTimeInt64() instead of
     sqlite3OsCurrentTimeInt64(db->pVfs, ...);
  2. a private ChaCha20 PRNG, seeded like SQLITE_TESTCTRL_PRNG_SEED seeds the
     global one, behind random(), randomblob(), random rowids (OP_NewRowid
     after MAX_ROWID), result-column-name dedup suffixes (which can reach
     CREATE TABLE AS) and the "Initialize data repository" seed-commit nonce;
     pager, WAL and VACUUM randomness keeps using the global PRNG, so it can
     no longer perturb the deterministic stream;
  3. UTC as the local timezone ('localtime' and 'utc' modifiers);
  4. optionally last_insert_rowid() and changes() reset to 0.

The seed commit of a NEW prolly store is written inside sqlite3_open_v2,
before the caller holds a handle. The open-time URI parameters
doltlite_det_ms=<unix ms> and doltlite_det_seed=<integer> pin it, so two
independently created stores get the same genesis hash.

Checked while writing this (0.51.11): dolt_commit --date already carries an
explicit "has timestamp" flag, so --date 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z (epoch 0) is not
treated as unset; the zero-timestamp sentinel the design note describes was in
0.11.x. Not patched: vec1 (the ANN module seeds its k-means from the global
PRNG, so the celld authorizer profile denies it) and the FTS5 per-connection
locale header (fts5_locale() is denied likewise).

